extraction_notes: "WB30 D-Bees of North America printed 37-40 (cache p038-p041), numbers read off 200 dpi renders. A reprint; the book notes it originally appeared in Rifts World Book One: Vampire Kingdoms, which is not imported, so it is imported from here. The brief listed 37-39; Money and the end of Standard Equipment are on printed 40, so source_book cites 37-40. Tag line: Bruutasaur - Optional Player Character or NPC. || CATEGORY: a full R.C.C. with its own skills, related and secondary skills; it states mdc_base, so no men_of_arms line. || XP TABLE: the entry says Use the same Experience Table as Psi-Stalkers. Stored as a copy of the psi-stalker class''s stored xp_table, read from production 2026-10-03, by the class-import reference rule (a class whose book names another class''s table copies that ladder). The shared brief for this book said no xp_table, on the premise that entries name the O.C.C.''s table; this one names a class, so the copy was taken. || ATTRIBUTES: P.S. 4D6+6 is Robotic; Spd 3D6+18, twice as fast in bursts of 1D4 minutes (ability text). || POOLS: M.D.C. 2D6x10 plus P.E. attribute number to start, plus 10 M.D.C. per level. Horror Factor 13. P.P.E. 3D6. No Hit Points or S.D.C. are printed. || SKILLS: printed base plus bonus over the catalog base: Language Other 50+10=60, Appraise Goods 30+15=45, Barter 30+12=42, Climbing 40+30=70, Land Navigation 36+20=56, Recognize Weapon Quality 25+20=45, Spelunking 35+20=55, Swimming 50+10=60, Tracking (people) 25+10=35, Track & Trap Animals 20+20=40, Wilderness Survival 30+20=50. Hunting has no percentage. Adopted Native Tongue Spanish 92% is Language: Native Tongue base 92. W.P. Ancient (3) and W.P. Modern (4) are from-lists of the catalog''s ancient and modern W.P. rows. Hand to Hand Basic; Expert costs one R.C.C. Related Skill, Martial Arts or Commando two; stored in hand_to_hand. || RELATED: five at level one plus one at levels 2, 4, 8, 10, 12 and 14. Communications is Language and Radio: Basic only at +5% and Literacy at -10%; the catalog files Language: Other under Technical, so Technical is granted with only Language: Other, and the Literacy penalty is a restriction line because one category carries one bonus. Rogue excludes Computer Hacking, Prowl and Safe-Cracking; the catalog files Prowl under Physical, so Prowl is excluded there beside Acrobatics. Pilot is basic vehicles only, including Hovercycle; the from-list of basic vehicles is a judgement. Science is Math: Basic only (catalog Mathematics: Basic). || SECONDARY: two at levels 1, 4, 8 and 12. || BONUSES: +2 attacks per melee, +1 initiative, +2 strike, +1 parry and dodge, +1 disarm, +3 pull punch, +2 roll with impact, +3 save vs Horror Factor, +6 save vs vampire charm and control (saves.other); impervious to vampire bite is ability text. || EQUIPMENT: backpack, 1D4 large sacks, ammo belt, two canteens or water skins, air filter, a week of food rations, 1D4+4 wooden stakes, a wooden mallet, a hand-held wooden cross (two feet for them, large-wood-cross), 1D4+4 E-Clips or ammo cartridges, a few personal items. The 72 silver bullets if an S.D.C. gun is one of the W.P.s are conditional and not stored; the backpack and/or large satchel is stored as backpack. Starts with no Techno-Wizard device or magic weapon. Armor examples (patchwork 5D6+55 M.D.C., medium full-body 1D4x10+80, heavy 1D6x10+140) are prose, not gear. || MONEY: 1D6x1,000 credits stored; an additional 2D4x1,000 credits of tradeable goods is not money and is not stored. || NOT STORED: size 10-12 ft, weight 850-1200 lbs, life span 2D6+40 years, NPC experience level 1D10, habitat, slave market value 2D4x10,000 credits, allies and enemies (a century-long feud with the Simvan; hunters of vampires)."
